audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    '|a||Why and because in Russian: потому что':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5120
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Tom has news: a job in Petersburg. Ask why with почему́, answer with потому́ что, and draw the result with поэ́тому.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:15029s6'
    '|a||Ло́ндон, а́вгуст. I''ve got big news, and I''m phoning Masha in Moscow.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Послу́шайте: listen first; the words come later. What is my news?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1y9ce34'
    '|a||Ма́ша, у меня́ но́вость! Мне предложи́ли рабо́ту в Петербу́рге, и я реши́л: я переезжа́ю!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1gc2b48'
    '|b||Пра́вда? Почему́ в Петербу́рге?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2920
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Потому́ что там но́вый рестора́н. Я хочу́ там рабо́тать, поэ́тому ско́ро я бу́ду жить в Петербу́рге!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Как хорошо́! Тепе́рь у тебя́ но́вая жизнь!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3760
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Where is Tom''s new job?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2320
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||В Петербу́рге: in Petersburg.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3000
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Why Petersburg?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Там но́вый рестора́н: there''s a new restaurant there.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3640
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||From today I say these in Russian: пра́вильно, молоде́ц, вы́берите, запо́лните про́пуски.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8720
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Посмотри́те. Masha asked: почему́ в Петербу́рге? Почему́ is why.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:c0a7ei'
    '|a||And I answered: потому́ что там но́вый рестора́н. Потому́ что is because.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1q44hm7'
    '|a||Then: я хочу́ там рабо́тать, поэ́тому ско́ро я бу́ду жить в Петербу́рге. Поэ́тому is so, that''s why.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:jde4un'
    '|a||Both answer почему́. The difference is the order.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:4sgqk5'
    '|a||Там но́вый рестора́н, поэ́тому я переезжа́ю. The cause first, then поэ́тому, then the result.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:nelq2c'
    '|a||Я переезжа́ю, потому́ что там но́вый рестора́н. The result first; потому́ что brings in the cause.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1dnm524'
    '|a||Same news, same comma; only the order turns round. And all three start with по: почему́, потому́ что, поэ́тому.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:7ofmqx'
    '|a||У меня́ но́вость! I''ve got news: но́вость, from но́вый, new.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:qleiq7'
    '|a||Мне предложи́ли рабо́ту: they offered me a job.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1sm85b8'
    '|a||There''s no they: Russian uses the они́ form alone when it doesn''t matter who.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:jnwebl'
    '|a||Я реши́л: I decided. Masha would say я реши́ла.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1m3cm03'
    '|a||And я переезжа́ю: I''m moving, to a new home.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1qdtbpz'
    '|a||Ско́ро я бу́ду жить в Петербу́рге.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1l6p7jp'
    '|a||Тепе́рь is now in the sense of from now on; сейча́с is this very minute.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:rw1686'
    '|b||Тепе́рь у тебя́ но́вая жизнь!':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2480
      voice: 'gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated #ctx:b82p4h'
    '|a||Masha''s right: но́вая жизнь.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:14x5stu'
    '|a||Да́льше: the rest of the call. Then tap Practise after the dialogue.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:lm2ux6'
    '|a||Запо́лните про́пуски: потому́ что or поэ́тому? Look where the cause is.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:m9m87j'
    '|a||Запо́лните про́пуски.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1w5263r'
    '|a||Я учу́ ру́сский, потому́ что я переезжа́ю.':
